---
const details = [
  { title: 'Your style, from the start', body: 'Choose Classic or Gala, then make it yours with your colours, photographs and words.' },
  { title: 'A welcome just for them', body: 'Households enter their own code and see the celebrations they are invited to.' },
  { title: 'The details, beautifully gathered', body: 'Give guests the dates, places and dress codes they need, right inside your invitation.' },
]
---
<section id="features" class="invitation-section section-wrap section-space" aria-labelledby="invitation-heading">
  <div class="section-heading" data-reveal>
    <h2 id="invitation-heading" class="display">The first glimpse<br />of your day.</h2>
    <p>Set the feeling before the celebrations begin. An invitation that looks, reads and feels like the two of you.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="design-gallery" data-reveal>
    <figure class="design-classic">
      <div class="design-image"><img src="/images/classic.webp" width="900" height="1200" loading="lazy" alt="Classic invitation design with centred names over a sunlit wedding photograph" /></div>
      <figcaption><h3>Classic</h3><p>A timeless, considered welcome.</p><span>Included with Ivory</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="design-gala">
      <div class="design-image"><img src="/images/gala.webp" width="900" height="1200" loading="lazy" alt="Gala invitation design with an editorial layout for the example wedding of Isla and Elliot" /></div>
      <figcaption><h3>Gala</h3><p>A little more expression.</p><span>Included with Ivory</span></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <dl class="invitation-details" data-reveal>{details.map(detail => <div><dt>{detail.title}</dt><dd>{detail.body}</dd></div>)}</dl>
</section>
